 {"id": "5fcf54a9c33a", "title": "Deduplicate Telegram bot subscribe/keyboard logic in telegram_bot.py", "description": "`app/core/telegram_bot.py` has significant duplication:\n\n1. `subscribe_to_endpoint_callback` (lines ~325-409) and `subscribe_to_endpoint` (lines ~411-483) implement almost the same subscribe-or-activate logic against two different Update surfaces (callback query vs message). The only real difference is which reply method is called and how the endpoint is fetched.\n2. `subscribe_command` (~150-196) and `refresh_endpoints_callback` (~525-566) both build an identical inline keyboard from the endpoint list and post the identical message text.\n3. `handler_command` for `/unsubscribe` is currently wired to `list_subscriptions_command` \u2014 probably a copy/paste bug but confirm before changing behavior; if intentional, add a short comment noting so.\n\n## What to change (ONLY this file)\n1. Extract `_upsert_subscription(cur, endpoint_id: int, chat_id: str) -> tuple[str, str]` returning `(status, endpoint_name)` where status is one of `\"already\"`, `\"reactivated\"`, `\"created\"`. Both `subscribe_to_endpoint_callback` and `subscribe_to_endpoint` should call it and pick the right reply text from a small dict.\n2. Extract `_build_endpoint_keyboard(endpoints: list[dict]) -> InlineKeyboardMarkup` and `_ENDPOINT_LIST_TEXT: str` module constants; use them in both `subscribe_command` and `refresh_endpoints_callback`.\n3. For the `/unsubscribe` handler wiring: if it is a bug (users expect unsubscribe, not list), rewire to a new small handler that shows only unsubscribe buttons. If preserving old behavior, add a `# NOTE: /unsubscribe intentionally reuses /list to show the unsubscribe buttons inline.` comment on that line.\n4. Preserve every user-facing message string exactly. No emoji or wording drift.\n5. Do not touch the DB schema, other modules, or add tests (Task 1 owns tests).\n\n## Files you own\n`app/core/telegram_bot.py` \u2014 nothing else.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `grep -c \"_upsert_subscription\" app/core/telegram_bot.py` returns >= 3 (definition + 2 call sites).\n- `grep -c \"_build_endpoint_keyboard\" app/core/telegram_bot.py` returns >= 3.\n- `python -c \"import app.core.telegram_bot\"` exits 0.\n- Net line count of the file drops by at least 80 lines vs before (there is ~180 lines of duplicate code).", "role": "backend", "priority": 2, "scope": "medium", "complexity": "medium", "estimated_minutes": 720, "status": "done", "task_type": "standard", "upgrade_details": null, "depends_on": [], "parent_task_id": null, "depends_on_repo": null, "owned_files": [], "assigned_agent": null, "result_summary": "Completed: Deduplicate Telegram bot subscribe/keyboard logic in telegram_bot.py", "tenant_id": "default", "cell_id": null, "repo": null, "batch_eligible": false, "eu_ai_act_risk": "minimal", "approval_required": false, "risk_level": "low", "slack_context": null, "version": 3, "claimed_at": 1786298577.122356, "completed_at": 1786298659.9142292, "closed_at": null, "claimed_by_session": "4163e54405e04cd9", "parent_session_id": null, "subtask_wait_started_at": null, "parent_context": null, "retry_count": 2, "max_retries": 3, "retry_delay_s": 30.0, "terminal_reason": null, "max_output_tokens": null, "meta_messages": ["Retry 1: Previous attempt failed with reason: Agent backend-c1a0df4d died; janitor failed: ['file_contains: app/core/telegram_bot.py :: _upsert_subscription (not found)', 'file_contains: app/core/telegram_bot.py :: _build_endpoint_keyboard (not found)', 'test_passes: python -c \"import app.core.telegram_bot\" (non-zero exit)']"], "metadata": {"budget_multiplier": 1.0, "original_task_id": "243fc900fa9b", "retry_mode": "cold", "retry_requested_mode": "warm", "retry_decision_hash": "9b9c00e08236d9149316b797b67d22da3d8676c3f2b2f783a0ac4e1b8fd74b54", "retry_downgrade_reason": "no_checkpoint"}, "max_turns": null}
