+{"id": "34196aa87c4d", "title": "Introduce repositories/DAL layer (new files only, no caller changes)", "description": "Every module in the codebase repeats the same `with get_db_connection() as conn: cur = conn.cursor(); cur.execute(...); rows = cur.fetchall()` boilerplate. Introduce a repository layer that centralizes SQL, returns plain dicts/dataclasses, and can be swapped/mocked in tests.\n\n## Scope of THIS task\nOnly create NEW files under `app/repositories/`. Do NOT edit any existing files (endpoints.py, telegram_bot.py, notifications.py, monitoring.py, etc.) \u2014 a follow-up task will migrate callers. Keeping this task file-disjoint prevents merge conflicts with concurrent refactoring work.\n\n## What to build\n1. `app/repositories/__init__.py` \u2014 re-exports the public repository functions.\n2. `app/repositories/endpoints.py` \u2014 `list_endpoints()`, `get_endpoint(id)`, `create_endpoint(name, url)`, `update_endpoint(id, name, url)`, `delete_endpoint(id)`, `update_status(id, status, checked_at)`, `mark_down(id, notified_at)`, `mark_up(id, notified_at)`, `update_notified(id, notified_at)`. Raise a small exception hierarchy: `EndpointNotFound`, `EndpointAlreadyExists` (wraps sqlite3.IntegrityError with a nicer message).\n3. `app/repositories/subscriptions.py` \u2014 `list_subscriptions_for_endpoint(endpoint_id)`, `list_subscriptions_for_chat(chat_id)`, `get_subscription(id)`, `create_subscription(endpoint_id, chat_id, enabled=True)`, `toggle_subscription(id)`, `delete_subscription(id)`, `get_enabled_chat_ids_for_endpoint(endpoint_id)`.\n4. `app/repositories/notification_logs.py` \u2014 `log_notification(endpoint_url, message, status, timestamp)`, `list_logs(page, per_page, sort_by, order, search, endpoint_filter, status_filter) -> (rows, total_count)`.\n5. `app/repositories/settings.py` \u2014 `get_all()`, `update(key, value)`. (Do not touch existing `app/db.py:get_settings` \u2014 that shim will be replaced later.)\n6. `app/repositories/discovery.py` \u2014 `find_pending(code)`, `mark_completed(id, chat_id, username, first_name, last_name)`, `create(code, expires_at, created_at)`.\n\n## Conventions\n- All functions accept required IDs as arguments and use `app.db.get_db_connection()` internally.\n- All read functions return `list[dict]` or `dict | None`; boolean 0/1 columns are cast to Python bool.\n- All write functions return the affected id (or None) and call `conn.commit()` inside their own `with` block.\n- Use type hints everywhere.\n- Do NOT add any tests here \u2014 Task 1 owns the test tree.\n\n## Acceptance\nAll six repository files exist. `python -c \"from app.repositories import endpoints, subscriptions, notification_logs, settings, discovery\"` exits 0.", "role": "architect", "priority": 0, "scope": "large", "complexity": "medium", "estimated_minutes": 120, "status": "open", "task_type": "standard", "upgrade_details": null, "depends_on": [], "parent_task_id": null, "depends_on_repo": null, "owned_files": ["app/repositories/__init__.py", "app/repositories/endpoints.py", "app/repositories/subscriptions.py", "app/repositories/notification_logs.py", "app/repositories/settings.py", "app/repositories/discovery.py"], "assigned_agent": null, "result_summary": null, "tenant_id": "default", "cell_id": null, "repo": null, "batch_eligible": false, "eu_ai_act_risk": "limited", "approval_required": false, "risk_level": "medium", "slack_context": null, "version": 4, "claimed_at": null, "completed_at": null, "closed_at": null, "claimed_by_session": null, "parent_session_id": null, "subtask_wait_started_at": null, "parent_context": null, "retry_count": 0, "max_retries": 3, "retry_delay_s": 0.0, "terminal_reason": null, "max_output_tokens": null, "meta_messages": [], "metadata": {"janitor_reopen_count": 1}, "max_turns": null}
+{"id": "9c424e1782a9", "title": "Fix wrong type annotation in monitoring.py and unify dashboard message formatting", "description": "`app/core/monitoring.py` has a bug: `update_notification_time(cur: requests.structures.CaseInsensitiveDict, ...)` \u2014 that annotation is nonsense (it is a sqlite3 cursor, not an HTTP header dict). It compiles only because `requests.structures.CaseInsensitiveDict` happens to be importable, but static analysis and readers are misled.\n\nAlso, the three notification messages in `check_endpoints_loop` (`[OK] RECOVERED`, `[ALERT] DOWN`, `[WARNING] STILL DOWN`) all hand-format `\"...\n\nDashboard: {config.DASHBOARD_URL}\"` inline. Extract a small helper.\n\n## What to change (ONLY this file)\n1. Change the parameter annotation on `update_notification_time` from `requests.structures.CaseInsensitiveDict` to `sqlite3.Cursor`. Add `import sqlite3` at the top; drop the unused import chain if no other use of `requests.structures` remains (there is not one).\n2. Add a small local helper `_format_alert(kind: str, url: str, status: int) -> str` (module-private, above `check_endpoints_loop`) that returns the message with the dashboard footer. Use it in all three scenarios inside `check_endpoints_loop` so future footer changes happen in one place.\n3. Do not change any log strings, control flow, timing, or DB queries. Behavior must be byte-for-byte identical in message TEXT; only the assembly path changes.\n\n## Files you own\n`app/core/monitoring.py` \u2014 nothing else.\n\n## Acceptance\n- `grep -n \"CaseInsensitiveDict\" app/core/monitoring.py` returns nothing.\n- `grep -n \"import sqlite3\" app/core/monitoring.py` finds the new import.\n- `grep -n \"_format_alert\" app/core/monitoring.py` shows the helper is defined and called at least 3 times.\n- `python -c \"import app.core.monitoring\"` exits 0.", "role": "backend", "priority": 0, "scope": "small", "complexity": "low", "estimated_minutes": 120, "status": "open", "task_type": "standard", "upg